{%- comment -%}
  Paste this into the "Quadrant" tab of the weather-yr plugin's Edit Markup
  screen (separate from the "Full" tab's template.liquid). Compact version
  for small Mashup panes - just current temp + condition + today's range.

  Font-family is set inline to force smooth Inter instead of the default
  pixel font, scoped to just this plugin (see template.liquid for why).

  IMPORTANT LESSON (learned the hard way, twice): a Quadrant pane is only
  ~1/4 of the screen and is NOT wide enough for an icon + the temperature
  text sharing the same row. TRMNL centers a row's content, so when the
  row is wider than the pane, both edges get clipped off equally - which
  silently deletes the icons at the ends AND chops up the temperature text
  in the middle (this looked like a corrupt-PNG or font-size bug, but it
  is plain horizontal overflow/clipping - confirmed because the
  condition/H-L/rain-forecast text rows below, which are plain stacked
  text with no icon sharing the row, always rendered perfectly fine).
  An earlier commit (35fb824) already hit and fixed this exact issue once
  by switching to a column layout with the icon stacked ABOVE the
  temperature rather than beside it - keep that pattern. The rule for this
  file going forward: never put an <img> on the same row as the
  temperature value; icons only ever share a row with OTHER icons (narrow),
  never with value/text content.

  Layout: weather icon + clothing/rain icon(s) together in one icon-only
  row on top (sized big enough to actually read at a glance - 44px, up
  from an earlier too-small 28px that made them hard to tell apart), then
  the temperature alone on its own row, then text labels below. The
  temperature keeps a real TRMNL value--* class (value--base) rather than
  a custom inline font-size - an arbitrary font-size outside TRMNL's own
  pixel/bitmap-font size set corrupted the digits in earlier testing.
  44px x up to 3 icons + gaps is still comfortably narrower than the
  "H xx.x / L xx.x" text row below, which has always rendered fine, so
  this shouldn't reintroduce the row-overflow issue described above.

  Rain forecast text: current.rain_forecast_text ("Inget regn i sikte
  närmaste 60 min!", "Det börjar regna kl HH:MM idag!", or a "Lätt regn kl
  HH:MM-HH:MM" range while it's already raining - see fetch.mjs), centered
  below everything else.

  All icon <img> tags use class="image image--contain image-dither" - NOT
  just "image" - see template.liquid's matching comment for why (matches
  plugins/broforce's confirmed-working icon markup). That alone was NOT
  enough to fix this plugin's icons though (still just a placeholder blob
  after adding those classes) - every image anywhere in this whole repo
  that has ever rendered correctly (broforce's portrait, banksy's picture,
  even this plugin's own forecast-table icon) has always been a single
  lone <img>, never sitting directly next to another <img> as a flex
  sibling - which is exactly what this icon row used to do (up to 3 <img>
  tags side by side). So the icons are now each in their own <table> cell
  instead - matching the forecast table's proven "single <img> inside a
  <td>" pattern - rather than flex siblings in one <div class="layout
  layout--row">.
{%- endcomment -%}

<div class="layout layout--col layout--center gap--small" style="font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif;">
  <table class="table" style="border: none; width: auto; margin: 0 auto;">
    <tr>
      <td style="border: none; padding: 0 2px;"><img class="image image--contain image-dither" src="{{ current.icon_url }}" width="44" height="44" style="width: 44px; height: 44px;"></td>
      <td style="border: none; padding: 0 2px;"><img class="image image--contain image-dither" src="{{ current.clothing_icon_url }}" width="44" height="44" style="width: 44px; height: 44px;"></td>
      {% if current.needs_rain_gear %}
      <td style="border: none; padding: 0 2px;"><img class="image image--contain image-dither" src="{{ current.rain_gear_icon_url }}" width="44" height="44" style="width: 44px; height: 44px;"></td>
      {% endif %}
    </tr>
  </table>
  <div class="value value--base">{{ current.temperature }}°</div>
  <div class="label">{{ current.condition_text }}</div>
  <div class="description">H {{ today.high }}° / L {{ today.low }}°</div>
  <div class="description">{{ current.rain_forecast_text }}</div>
</div>

<div class="title_bar" style="font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif;">
  <span class="title">Alsjön</span>
  <span class="instance">{{ updated_display }}</span>
</div>
